<title>USA: IPO PRICING-General Cable at $21.</title>
<headline>IPO PRICING-General Cable at $21.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Company Name     General Cable Corp</p>
<p>   Priced At			     $21</p>
<p>   Estimated Pricing Range	$21-24</p>
<p>   Number of Shares	  16.9 million</p>
<p>   Underwriters		 Dillon Read</p>
<p>NOTE: General Cable was previously a wholly owned subsidiary of Wassall Netherlands Cable BV. All 16.9 million shares were offered by Wassal.</p>
<p>Of the total number of shares offered, 13.52 million were offered in the United States and Canada while 3.38 million were offered outside the United States and Canada.</p>
<p>The company develops and manufactures copper wire and cable products for the communications and electrical markets.</p>
<p>According to its prospectus, General Cable posted operating profit of $78.5 million on sales of $1.04 billion in 1996. It will not receive any proceeds from the IPO.</p>
<p>After the offering, Wassall will own about 30 percent of the outstanding shares, or about 20 percent if the U.S. underwriters' over-allotment option is exercised in full.</p>
</text>
